From 65f641a6732d3f0fa04416b97117ee3d484c5209 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 19:33:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix zmm-width vecreg flush + dest-liveness in aggregate
 store-forwarding
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two miscompiles found via the zlib-ng 2.2.4 suite (both remaining parts
of the real-world validation bundle; the inliner/peephole/loop-promote
fixes landed separately as PR#66):

1. flush_vecreg_liveout width bug (zlib-ng adler32_avx512 build break):
   the live-out flush assumed vec_live_regs only holds xmm names and
   emitted the SSE 'movdqu' for zmm/ymm registers — an illegal encoding
   the internal assembler rightly rejected ('movdqu: no AVX-512/EVEX
   form'). Emit vmovdqu64 / vmovdqu / movdqu by register class.

2. aggregate_copy_forward dest-liveness window (zlib-ng CRC corruption):
   forward_store_only_temporaries redirects every write of root up to
   the memcpy so it lands in dest EARLY. That is only sound if dest's
   old contents are provably dead throughout [first redirected use,
   copy): any read of dest's object in that window now observes the new
   value. zlib-ng's fold_1 register rotation
   (tmp=*c3; *c3=*c0; *c1=*c2; *c2=tmp) read c2's OLD value after the
   snapshot write was redirected into c2 — every crc32_fold_copy+fold
   pair with unaligned lengths produced a wrong CRC, so gzip-wrapped
   decompression of any stream larger than one inflate window failed
   with 'incorrect data check' (minigzip -d, gzread). The validation
   now rejects candidates whose dest object is referenced (read OR
   written) inside the window. Regression: agg_fwd_dest_liveness.c
   locks in the rotation shape.

PROOF (CC=lccc -O2):
  zlib-ng 2.2.4: configure+make clean (incl. AVX512 TUs); make test
  PASS; 64K/256K/1M/4M random gzip round-trips OK; system-gzip
  cross-decompression OK; fold_copy+fold split-length matrix
  (17/999, 16/1000, 15/17, ...) matches oneshot CRC for all pairs
  (was 8/11 MISMATCH).
  Full battery: 653 lib tests, 161 regressions, 50 correctness,
  86 linker, 240/240 differential fuzz, asm-diff clean.
  gzip 1.14 30/30, expat 2.7.3 2/2, sqlite 3.50.4 differential
  byte-identical vs system sqlite3.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
